TOUPPER(3)                     P32W Unix                      TOUPPER(3)

NAME
       toupper, tolower - convert the case of a letter

SYNOPSIS
       #include <ctype.h>

       int toupper(int c);
       int tolower(int c);

DESCRIPTION
       toupper returns the upper-case letter for a lower-case ASCII
       letter c, and tolower the lower-case letter for an upper-case
       one. Any other value, EOF included, is returned unchanged.

EXAMPLES
       for (p = s; *p; p++)
           *p = toupper(*p);

SEE ALSO
       ctype(3), isspace(3)

BUGS
       ASCII only: no locales. There are no _toupper or _tolower
       macros.
